\section{Beyond gradient descent, encoder depth and the near-collapse window}
\label{sec:ext}

The race assumes gradient descent, a one-layer encoder and that collapse is decided early; we leave each in turn: AdamW (\cref{sec:adamw}), a deep linear encoder (\cref{sec:deep}), weight-decay schedules, which act after capture (\cref{sec:sched}), and a direct test of the premise in the ViT (\cref{sec:e8}).
Every prediction was frozen before its held-out runs and scored once, with the count of \citet{demelocosta2026drive} ($\mu$ count) among the baselines where defined; \cref{tab:ext-tests} (\cref{app:ext}) lists every test and verdict.

